---
// A driver package's parts, which of them the deployed bundle holds, and which commands load the
// rest. The bundle's boundary is the point: derive/ stays outside it. Drawn with Starlight's
// colour variables so it follows the light and dark themes.
import Diagram from "./Diagram.astro";
---

<Diagram title="A driver package's parts" minWidth={580} maxWidth={880}>
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 880 560"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="driver-modules-title driver-modules-desc"
  >
    <title id="driver-modules-title">A driver package's parts</title>
    <desc id="driver-modules-desc">
      A driver package holds src/index.ts, what a configuration imports, src/types.ts, the
      vocabulary both halves use, and three folders: config/, runtime/ and derive/. The
      deployed bundle, .gen/runtime/bundle.mjs, follows every import from the generated entry
      point, entry.js. entry.js imports gateway.config.ts, which imports the driver's
      src/index.ts, which imports config/. config/ reaches runtime/ only through
      createExecutor's dynamic import, which the bundler also follows. So the bundle holds
      src/index.ts, src/types.ts, config/ and runtime/. config/ names derive/ only by a file:
      URL, deriveSchemasModule, which the bundler never follows, so derive/ is outside the
      bundle. gateway-codegen and gateway-schemas both load config/ and derive/: codegen loads
      config/ when it loads a configuration, and derive/ with the network refused, and
      gateway-schemas uses the network. The driver's eslint.config.ts refuses imports from
      config/ and src/*.ts into runtime/ or derive/, from runtime/ into derive/, and from
      derive/ into runtime/, though runtime/'s types may cross.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker
        id="driver-modules-arrow"
        viewBox="0 0 10 10"
        refX="9"
        refY="5"
        markerWidth="7"
        markerHeight="7"
        orient="auto-start-reverse"
      >
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="head"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- Driver package -->
    <rect class="section" x="40" y="140" width="826" height="250" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="section-title" x="56" y="168">Driver package</text>

    <!-- The deployed bundle, drawn over the package it cuts across -->
    <rect class="bundle" x="30" y="10" width="530" height="390" rx="12"></rect>
    <text class="title bundle-title" x="46" y="38">The deployed bundle</text>
    <text class="note mono" x="232" y="37">.gen/runtime/bundle.mjs</text>

    <rect class="box" x="50" y="60" width="200" height="56" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label mono" x="150" y="84">entry.js</text>
    <text class="sub" x="150" y="104">the generated entry point</text>

    <rect class="box" x="330" y="60" width="220" height="56" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label mono" x="440" y="84">gateway.config.ts</text>
    <text class="sub" x="440" y="104">the gateway's configuration</text>

    <rect class="box" x="50" y="186" width="200" height="56" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label mono" x="150" y="210">src/types.ts</text>
    <text class="sub" x="150" y="230">vocabulary both halves use</text>

    <rect class="box" x="330" y="186" width="220" height="56" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label mono" x="440" y="210">src/index.ts</text>
    <text class="sub" x="440" y="230">what a configuration imports</text>

    <rect class="box" x="50" y="290" width="200" height="76" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label mono" x="150" y="316">runtime/</text>
    <text class="sub" x="150" y="337">the executor, loaded by</text>
    <text class="sub" x="150" y="354">createExecutor on first call</text>

    <rect class="box" x="330" y="290" width="220" height="76" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label mono" x="440" y="316">config/</text>
    <text class="sub" x="440" y="337">definition · check · handler</text>
    <text class="sub" x="440" y="354">no network, secret or environment</text>

    <rect class="box accent" x="620" y="290" width="230" height="76" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label mono" x="735" y="316">derive/</text>
    <text class="sub" x="735" y="337">named by deriveSchemasModule,</text>
    <text class="sub" x="735" y="354">a file: URL · never bundled</text>

    <!-- What loads config/ and derive/ -->
    <rect class="box" x="330" y="476" width="220" height="56" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label mono" x="440" y="500">gateway-codegen</text>
    <text class="sub" x="440" y="520">derive/ with the network refused</text>

    <rect class="box" x="620" y="476" width="230" height="56" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label mono" x="735" y="500">gateway-schemas</text>
    <text class="sub" x="735" y="520">uses the network</text>

    <!-- What the driver's lint rule refuses -->
    <text class="label small start mono" x="50" y="440">eslint.config.ts</text>
    <text class="note" x="50" y="462">refuses these imports:</text>
    <text class="note" x="50" y="482">config/, src/*.ts → runtime/, derive/</text>
    <text class="note" x="50" y="502">runtime/ → derive/</text>
    <text class="note" x="50" y="522">derive/ → runtime/</text>
    <text class="note" x="50" y="542">but runtime/'s types may cross</text>

    <!-- Imports the bundler follows -->
    <line class="flow" x1="250" y1="88" x2="328" y2="88"></line>
    <line class="flow" x1="440" y1="116" x2="440" y2="184"></line>
    <line class="flow" x1="440" y1="242" x2="440" y2="288"></line>
    <line class="flow dashed" x1="330" y1="328" x2="252" y2="328"></line>

    <!-- A name, not an import -->
    <line class="link" x1="550" y1="328" x2="618" y2="328"></line>
    <text class="note" x="590" y="320" text-anchor="middle">URL</text>

    <!-- Loaders -->
    <line class="bus" x1="440" y1="436" x2="735" y2="436"></line>
    <line class="bus" x1="440" y1="476" x2="440" y2="436"></line>
    <line class="bus" x1="735" y1="476" x2="735" y2="436"></line>
    <line class="flow" x1="440" y1="436" x2="440" y2="368"></line>
    <line class="flow" x1="735" y1="436" x2="735" y2="368"></line>
    <text class="note" x="588" y="428" text-anchor="middle">both load</text>
  </svg>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    Solid arrows are imports. The dashed one is createExecutor's dynamic import, which the bundler
    follows too. The dotted line is a URL, which it never follows.
  </Fragment>
</Diagram>

<style>
  .flow {
    marker-end: url(#driver-modules-arrow);
  }
  .bundle {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--sl-color-accent);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-dasharray: 8 4;
  }
  .bundle-title {
    fill: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
  }
  .link {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-dasharray: 2 4;
  }
</style>
